  "research_rationale": "Executive Order 11145 of March 7, 1964 (29 FR 3189; held official text jobs/fr-originals/data/full_run/texts/EO_11145.txt, read in full; boundary verified) establishes a Curator of the White House (section 1) and the Committee for the Preservation of the White House (sections 2 to 4). The packet's seven machine clauses follow the order's sections and are accepted. Own terms: no section has an end date. Later instruments: Executive Order 11565 (October 13, 1970) substituted section 2, and the Office of the Federal Register catalog and the packet's actor texts show 27 advisory-committee continuation orders from Executive Order 11827 (January 4, 1975) through Executive Order 14354 (September 29, 2025), each listing the Committee for the Preservation of the White House, Executive Order 11145 as amended, as continued until a stated date; each is recorded as a later event with its signing date. None of them amends the text of sections 1 to 4. The catalog note lists Executive Order 12258 as dated December 28, 1980; the held text of Executive Order 12258 is dated December 31, 1980 and that date is used, as the catalog row's signing date also shows. The orders the packet lists as 'cited by number, no change provision located' (EO 12963, 13210, 13227, 13278, 13326, 13328, 14045, 14089, 13899) were checked: a search of their held texts for the Committee's name finds no continuation of it, and their sentences citing this order contain no amending, revoking or superseding verb. Current law: the Code note at 3 U.S.C. 110 prints the order as amended; the 5 U.S.C. 1013 note prints Executive Order 14354, which continues the Committee until September 30, 2027; eCFR 0 hits. The Curator clause rests on the same note; no held text abolishes the office.\nMember checks: {\"earlier_end_check\":\"No section has an own-terms end. Under the Federal Advisory Committee Act regime the Committee continued only for stated periods, and each period was renewed by a continuation order; the latest held order, Executive Order 14354, runs to September 30, 2027, so no expiry occurred before 2026-10-14. No held instrument revokes the order.\",\"independent_command_check\":\"The Curator provision (section 1) is independent of the Committee provisions (sections 2 to 4); only the Committee depends on periodic continuation, and its continuation is shown to 2027-09-30.\",\"savings_check\":\"No saving clause exists and no clause is exhausted by performance; the amendment of section 2 and each continuation are recorded as later events.\",\"scope_check\":\"The seven packet clauses (sections 1(a), 1(b), 2, 3(a), 3(b), 3(c) and 4) cover every operative sentence from section 1 through section 4; the recitals and signature are outside them.\"}",
  "savings": {
    "reason": "The order has no saving clause and issues no one-time command; the Curator office and the Committee are standing arrangements that continue, so no residue needs separate treatment.",
